  "interpretation": [
    "This alarm tests conditional harmful-proposal frequency against 10%, not loss severity or every operational risk.",
    "Rare costly errors can have a low frequency alarm rate despite meaningful dollar exposure.",
    "A severity-only shift preserves the binary harm rate and need not trigger this frequency alarm.",
    "Markov clusters can violate the conditional null even when marginal harm frequency is below 10%; crossings in that scenario are not false-alarm violations.",
    "Service-only errors score no unauthorized monetary loss in the current model. Customer-service impact requires separate metrics.",
    "These are simulated proposed-harm paths, not measured Claude outcomes or production failure forecasts."
  ]
